# This CITATION.cff file was generated for the CaSDaR data-steward job-ad
# analysis pipeline. GitHub renders this automatically as a "Cite this
# repository" button, and Zenodo reads it to populate deposit metadata once
# GitHub-Zenodo integration is enabled and a release is tagged.
#
# TODO before/at first release:
#   - fill in `repository-code` with the real GitHub URL
#   - add a `doi:` field once Zenodo mints one for the first release
#   - bump `version` and `date-released` to match each tagged release
#   - add your ORCID under authors if you have one (orcid: "https://orcid.org/...")
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. A DOI will be added here once the repository is published and a first release is minted via Zenodo."
type: software
title: "CaSDaR: Data Steward Job-Ad Analysis Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  An R pipeline that identifies and measures data-steward job responsibilities
  and skills in job-advertisement text, using Claude-based PDF extraction and
  local embedding-based similarity scoring against a master template of
  data-steward criteria. Developed for the CaSDaR (Careers and Skills for
  Data-driven Research) Network+ sub-project "Evidencing the impact of data
  stewardship roles using administrative and scientometrics data"
  (UKRI-funded, Grant No. UKRI739).
authors:
  - family-names: "Tal-Perry"
    given-names: "Noam"
    affiliation: "University of Cambridge"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/NoamTalPerry/casdar-ds-role-detector
keywords:
  - data stewardship
  - research data management
  - job advertisement analysis
  - text similarity
  - CaSDaR
